        <briefdescription>
<para>Apply cached AMS trim data to the FPD system monitors. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Walks the four FPD system-monitor indices and applies the trim data for the FPD power domain. A missing monitor is reported as a warning and skipped; an error from trim application stops the walk. The final loop-index check detects an abnormal loop termination.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>PwrDomain</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unused power-domain callback argument. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Args</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unused callback argument array. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>NumOfArgs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unused number of callback arguments.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS after all present monitors are processed (including when monitors are absent); an error returned by XPm_ApplyAmsTrim(); or XST_GLITCH_ERROR if the loop does not reach its expected terminal index. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Check if i is reach to XPM_NODEIDX_MONITOR_SYSMON_FPD_3 + 1 </para>        </inbodydescription>
